Material Color Utilities attribution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sources/PaletteColor/MaterialColorUtilities/ is vendored from the Swift port in
material-foundation/material-color-utilities at commit
5b3618b16fdc3825e21d5679bafd144662088ea1:
https://github.com/material-foundation/material-color-utilities/tree/5b3618b16fdc3825e21d5679bafd144662088ea1/swift/Sources/MaterialColorUtilities

Files: Cam16.swift, ColorUtils.swift, Hct.swift, HctSolver.swift,
MathUtils.swift, PointProvider.swift, PointProviderLab.swift, Quantizer.swift,
QuantizerCelebi.swift, QuantizerMap.swift, QuantizerWsmeans.swift,
QuantizerWu.swift, Score.swift, TonalPalette.swift, ViewingConditions.swift.

Local modifications:

  - All declarations reduced from `public` to internal and `@inlinable`
    removed, so the copy does not collide with the upstream module.
  - QuantizerWsmeans.swift: the `debug` static var and debug logging were
    removed (a mutable static is not concurrency-safe under Swift's strict
    concurrency checking); `DistanceAndIndex.==` now compares equal distances
    rather than unequal ones.
  - QuantizerWu.swift: an unmutated `var` was changed to `let`.
  - A provenance header was prepended to each file.

Sources/PaletteColor/MediaArtworkScheme.swift follows the
`CorePalettesContent` palette formulas from SchemeContent.swift in the same
tree and the media-control role tones used by Android SystemUI.

